.TH smi-nginx-fix-content "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-nginx-fix-content \- Set owners, modes and SELinux labels of the served nginx content
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-nginx-fix-content
.RB [ \-n ]
.RI [ DIRECTORY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-nginx-fix-content
makes the served files readable by nginx: owner
.BR root:root ,
.B 0755
for directories,
.B 0644
for files, and the SELinux labels restored with
.B restorecon -RF
when
.BR restorecon (8)
is installed.
.PP
Without
.I DIRECTORY
it works on the content trees of the web front:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/usr/share/nginx/vhosts
/usr/share/nginx/brands
/usr/share/nginx/apps
/usr/share/nginx/errors
/usr/share/nginx/acme
.fi
.RE
.PP
A tree that does not exist is skipped.
.B draft
folders below those trees are included, so a new build copied into
.IB name /draft
is served with the same rights as a released one.
.PP
Symbolic links keep their own path but are given the owner of the tree, because nginx refuses a
link whose owner differs from its target.
Anything that is neither a regular file, a directory nor a symbolic link is reported and left
alone, and so is a link pointing nowhere.
Each such finding is counted, and the command ends with
.B 1
when any are left, after having done the rest of the work.
.PP
A missing
.I /usr/share/nginx/html
is reported as well; nginx needs it.
.PP
Run it after copying a build, after releasing a draft, and whenever a page answers
.B 404
for no visible reason.
It has to be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run: print the commands that would change something, prefixed with
.BR "would run" ,
and change nothing. The checks still run and are still reported.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I DIRECTORY
One absolute directory to fix instead of all the trees. It must exist.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Everything was set and nothing was found to report.
.TP
.B 1
Not root, an unknown option, a relative or missing
.IR DIRECTORY ,
or findings were reported.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Everything, after a deployment:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-nginx-fix-content
.fi
.RE
.PP
One tree, looking first:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-nginx-fix-content -n /usr/share/nginx/apps
sudo smi-nginx-fix-content /usr/share/nginx/apps
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
